                            {
                                "example_id": "f03be77b-a74a-43ac-ae64-9db1a6573153",
                                "sense_id": "f3245627-2a78-3318-9042-4b65f25a9390",
                                "text": "Petrosilex has given rise to different ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f6d84b68-ae92-44b8-b215-82b5918516bc",
                                "sense_id": "f3245627-2a78-3318-9042-4b65f25a9390",
                                "text": "The name simple petrosilex seems to have been confined to the more apparenttly homogeneous felsites, while the term porphyritic petrosilex was given to those rocks supposed to have a base of simple petrosilex or of felsparoid which held enclosed porphyritic crystals."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd11060f-7981-4f05-a5c4-488f4b8c90e0",
                                "sense_id": "f3245627-2a78-3318-9042-4b65f25a9390",
                                "text": "A brief history of the word felsite and its synonyms in different countries (petrosilex, eurite, and ha:lleflinta) will serve to illustrate the unfitness of it and these allied terms for exact petrographical usage."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "865a4496-fe01-35a6-b83b-e994fe0d7586",
                        "entry_id": "a99cfec0-c155-39b2-b0e3-b01850495f8e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A fine-grained, silica-rich rock composed of quartz and sometimes other minerals, similar to the chemical structure of hornstone but having a different texture."
